Ladybird’s UA link rules now match HTML elements only, so an SVG <a>
keeps its text-decoration none and its color. Blink and WebKit do the
same: Both of their html.css style sheets declare the XHTML namespace as
the default one. Gecko’s html.css does too, but Firefox still colors an
SVG link with LinkText, though it doesn’t underline it. In Chrome
158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 (engine-compare), an SVG
<a> computes text-decoration-line none and cursor pointer, and its color
is black in Chrome and WebKit.

MathML links keep the link color: Blink’s mathml.css gives a:-webkit-
any-link the -webkit-link color, and WebKit’s gives :any-link the same,
both without an underline. Ladybird’s MathML style sheet now colors them
itself, rather than through the HTML rules.
